# Trivy ignore list — scanned by the `docker` job in .github/workflows/ci.yml
# (backend runtime image, HIGH/CRITICAL, ignore-unfixed).
#
# The backend image ships Prisma's CLI dependency chain even though the
# container never executes it: @prisma/client 7 declares `prisma` and
# `typescript` as optional peers, npm keeps them in the pruned production
# tree, and prisma pins its own transitive deps.
#
#   CVE-2026-40345 — deepmerge-ts 7.1.5 stack exhaustion (fixed in 8.0.0)
#     via @prisma/config ← prisma CLI. Only used to merge prisma.config.ts
#     at build/CLI time; the container CMD is `node dist/src/index.js` and
#     database access goes through @prisma/adapter-pg (PostgreSQL), so this
#     code path never runs inside the image.
#
#   GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr / GHSA-rgwj-5xj2-c3m3 — mysql2 auth-plugin
#     downgrade (plaintext credential leak) via prisma CLI's bundled MySQL
#     driver. This project is PostgreSQL-only; mysql2 is unreachable, and
#     prisma pins it to exactly 3.15.3, so there is no upgrade path until
#     prisma >7.10.0 moves its pin (same chain is allowlisted in the npm
#     audit gates in this workflow).
#
# Neither package is reachable from application code at runtime.
CVE-2026-40345
GHSA-3f6p-5ww8-9rcr
GHSA-rgwj-5xj2-c3m3
